{"term":"tilt","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:63760d17892813fc6b","definition":"To slope or incline (something); to slant.","example":"Tilt the barrel to pour out its contents.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7af0ec014c6dda2b25","definition":"To be at an angle.","example":"For as the Trunk of the Body, is kept from tilting forvvard by the Muſcules of the Back: So, from falling backvvard, by theſe of the Belly.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e42a1958411e30c49a","definition":"To charge (at someone) with a lance.","example":"Auster and Aquilon with winged Steeds / All ſweating, tilt about the watery heauens, / With ſhiuering ſpeares enforcing thunderclaps, / And from their ſhields ſtrike flames of lightening","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2289c8dae579309096","definition":"To point or thrust a weapon at.","example":"And he should tilt her?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktiona