ughly to \"I am really mad because some idiot punched in some random lineup that ended up catching every conceivable break and beating me.\")","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f236f8df0d58d878b2","definition":"To modify one's approach.","example":"While self-checkout machines are often used alongside cashiers, labor unions say that tilting toward fully cashierless operations threatens the French way of life by encouraging American-style consumerism and automation, putting thousands of jobs at risk.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["slope","incline","slant","cock","cant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:09a2a52cb2568f2249","definition":"A slope or inclination.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["canthal tilt","I'm using tilt controls!"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a1c8a36d8cc1a8c3b","definition":"The inclination of part of the body, such as backbone, pelvis, head, etc.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["canthal tilt","I'm using tilt controls!"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktio